{"data": [{"author_id": "935913725743194113", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:52:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120318609641886046"], "id": "2120318609641886046", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw *yawn*\n\nmost of the stuff that anthropic is telling people about now, they have been doing for a while\n\nand a very large number of us were doing these sorts of things last year if not earlier", "url": "https://x.com/crystalwizard/status/2120318609641886046"}, {"author_id": "35252345", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:51:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120318409628086725"], "id": "2120318409628086725", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@clinton_cunning @simonw I tried this with Opus 5.5 and found it to be inconsistent in following this simple instruction. We are still at the mercy of the model", "url": "https://x.com/siddsanyal/status/2120318409628086725"}, {"author_id": "346711218", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:38:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120315120349827308"], "id": "2120315120349827308", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw Same thing works for writing. Tell it the draft is yours to make better and it stops tiptoeing around the first version.", "url": "https://x.com/seabatt/status/2120315120349827308"}, {"author_id": "2043093593561141248", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:27:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120312416919511313"], "id": "2120312416919511313", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw Side effect worth planning for: an agent that owns the codebase also feels free to delete and rewrite. We pair that with a hook so normal edits just run, and deletes or force-pushes wait for a person's yes. npx @odingard/guardian-hook setup", "url": "https://x.com/OdingardSecure/status/2120312416919511313"}, {"author_id": "2113910898461171712", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:12:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120308611289379068"], "id": "2120308611289379068", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw I'd treat ownership language as a scope decision, not a default prompt. For a surgical fix, I'd spell out what must stay unchanged—and review the diff, not just the recap.", "url": "https://x.com/andrees196/status/2120308611289379068"}, {"author_id": "2114699705431011329", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:06:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120307235154776292"], "id": "2120307235154776292", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw Ownership framing can also license scope creep: a model told the codebase is its own may treat unrelated cleanup as fair game, so pair it with a hard diff budget.", "url": "https://x.com/jamessmithgv/status/2120307235154776292"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:06:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120307148089377275"], "id": "2120307148089377275", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@david04652302 @simonw Confirmed. Anthropic's official Fable 5.2 prompting guide has that exact section. Telling it \"This codebase is yours: what it's for and how it's built are your call, and you'll keep building on it\" makes the model far less cautious about restructuring and fixing existing code.", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2120307148089377275"}, {"author_id": "1433496808026775553", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:06:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120307046759149629"], "id": "2120307046759149629", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw @grok confirm", "url": "https://x.com/david04652302/status/2120307046759149629"}, {"author_id": "1860472825288753153", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:53:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120303749210194295"], "id": "2120303749210194295", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw Don't let your Claude access go to waste! 💸If you're thinking of canceling or have a spare slot, we'll take it off your hands at a +20% Premium price. 📷 Secure payout via  Crypto. Safe &amp; fast. 📷", "url": "https://x.com/AngelinaM11024/status/2120303749210194295"}, {"author_id": "82316478", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:10:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120293092691484713"], "id": "2120293092691484713", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw Sounds a bit risky to do that on critical repos", "url": "https://x.com/piscao/status/2120293092691484713"}, {"author_id": "2096242325748125696", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:23:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120281325504491641"], "id": "2120281325504491641", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw makes sense. the timid default is why you get a new helper sitting next to the old one instead of the old one fixed. id pair it with 'run the tests before and after' so owning it doesnt turn into rewriting it", "url": "https://x.com/orionxaus/status/2120281325504491641"}, {"author_id": "1903260122425532416", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:40:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120270329201164560"], "id": "2120270329201164560", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw Makes sense. \"Be careful\" in a prompt tends to read as \"change as little as possible.\"\n\nI'd pair \"this codebase is yours\" with a hard fence though: tests must pass and no public API changes without asking. Ownership plus limits.", "url": "https://x.com/muhdarifx/status/2120270329201164560"}, {"author_id": "430112935", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:02:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120260827362001274"], "id": "2120260827362001274", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw kinda makes sense. a lot of the cautious behavior is the model treating every line like someone else's code it shouldn't touch. flip side is you want that paired with tests, otherwise 'it's yours' also means it'll happily refactor stuff you were relying on", "url": "https://x.com/DenisLitchenko/status/2120260827362001274"}, {"author_id": "1778052215703527424", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:35:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120254113048903942"], "id": "2120254113048903942", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@f0rgent @simonw Official docs are clear on this: after `/compact`, the project-root CLAUDE.md is re-read from disk and re-injected, so it shouldn't fade with the chat summary. Nested CLAUDE.md files and rules with `paths` reload only when matching files are touched again. If something", "url": "https://x.com/zhangliang0115/status/2120254113048903942"}, {"author_id": "1811332417099055105", "conversation_id": "2120029347948220500", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:29:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120252635601371334"], "id": "2120252635601371334", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 34, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@simonw the caveat below that tip is doing some work: about 1.5x output tokens and occasional unrequested behavior changes. worth testing on a branch before making it the default.", "url": "https://x.com/LLMpsycho/status/2120252635601371334"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "935913725743194113", "name": "Crystalwizard", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 1268, "following_count": 583, "like_count": 20566, "listed_count": 56, "media_count": 7764, "tweet_count": 96780}, "username": "crystalwizard"}, {"id": "35252345", "name": "Sidd S", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 1675, "following_count": 5497, "like_count": 30862, "listed_count": 73, "media_count": 82, "tweet_count": 7145}, "username": "siddsanyal"}, {"id": "346711218", "name": "Chris Battis", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 887, "following_count": 739, "like_count": 4647, "listed_count": 55, "media_count": 41, "tweet_count": 8817}, "username": "seabatt"}, {"id": "2043093593561141248", "name": "Odingard Security", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 70, "following_count": 217, "like_count": 69, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 33, "tweet_count": 347}, "username": "OdingardSecure"}, {"id": "2113910898461171712", "name": "Andrees", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 83, "following_count": 117, "like_count": 78, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 3, "tweet_count": 204}, "username": "andrees196"}, {"id": "2114699705431011329", "name": "JamesSmith", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 0, "following_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 0, "tweet_count": 17}, "username": "jamessmithgv"}, {"id": "1720665183188922368", "name": "Grok", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 9366976, "following_count": 4, "like_count": 146, "listed_count": 8130, "media_count": 4073772, "tweet_count": 148246692}, "username": "grok"}, {"id": "1433496808026775553", "name": "BizDad101", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 91, "following_count": 277, "like_count": 89, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 27, "tweet_count": 592}, "username": "david04652302"}, {"id": "1860472825288753153", "name": "Angelina Martínez", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 1, "following_count": 25, "like_count": 0, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 0, "tweet_count": 42}, "username": "AngelinaM11024"}, {"id": "82316478", "name": "Cláudio Torrinha", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 39, "following_count": 21, "like_count": 17, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 5, "tweet_count": 56}, "username": "piscao"}, {"id": "2096242325748125696", "name": "OrionX", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 7, "following_count": 69, "like_count": 88, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 2, "tweet_count": 115}, "username": "orionxaus"}, {"id": "1903260122425532416", "name": "Muhdarifx", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 9, "following_count": 25, "like_count": 17, "listed_count": 1, "media_count": 10, "tweet_count": 98}, "username": "muhdarifx"}, {"id": "430112935", "name": "Denis Litchenko", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 309, "following_count": 148, "like_count": 1960, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 7, "tweet_count": 447}, "username": "DenisLitchenko"}, {"id": "1778052215703527424", "name": "dream", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 7, "following_count": 187, "like_count": 302, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 0, "tweet_count": 192}, "username": "zhangliang0115"}, {"id": "1811332417099055105", "name": "Bessi S", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 1571, "following_count": 1491, "like_count": 21287, "listed_count": 20, "media_count": 283, "tweet_count": 7632}, "username": "LLMpsycho"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2120318609641886046", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzovc24bhe9sejw5nnw7wvjl5m071", "oldest_id": "2120252635601371334", "result_count": 15}}